\f0\b MOVEMENT AND PHYSICAL CONTINUITY
\f1\b0 \
All movements must have clear beginnings and endings. Show Aeri descending from the desk, contacting the floor, walking toward the sofa, climbing onto the cushion, and settling down in the correct order.\
Maintain believable contact, balance, weight, paw placement, furniture support, and ground shadows within the stylized animated world. The paper must move only when pushed. The bowl and leash must remain in place unless deliberately moved.\
Do not teleport Aeri between locations, skip the floor-level journey, or change the room layout between shots.\

\f0\b AUDIO AND PERFORMANCE
\f1\b0 \
Use clear, naturally timed English dialogue with distinct speaker turns. Aeri's delivery is dry, controlled, and authoritative; the owner's delivery is defensive and then genuinely surprised.\
Include subtle paper sliding, leash movement, paw steps, and sofa-cushion sounds where appropriate. Add a brief sitcom laugh track after the final reveal. No background music, narration, extra dialogue, or unnecessary vocalizations.\
Allow short pauses for reactions without exceeding the 10-second duration.\

\f0\b NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS
\f1\b0 \
No photorealistic live-action appearance, real-world photographic character rendering, live-action footage, or realistic human-and-animal filming aesthetic. No flat illustration, 2D cartoon rendering, toy-like plastic materials, or plush-doll appearance.\
No changes to Aeri's breed, canine anatomy, face, coat colors, proportions, clothing, or size. No inconsistent owner appearance or wardrobe. No extra characters, random props, unnecessary gestures, extra dialogue, subtitles, captions, watermarks, storyboard borders, arrows, timestamps, or inset images.\
Do not reproduce the storyboard as a visible grid. Generate a single coherent vertical video with continuous action, deliberate shot changes, consistent stylized 3D rendering, stable character identity, and a clear final comedic payoff.\
